Quick JS sample (streaming + function calling):

// pseudo-code, minimal example
import Redwood from 'redwood-sdk';
const client = new Redwood.Client({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY, streaming: true });

const res = await client.stream({
  model: 'redwood-stream-1',
  input: 'Suggest a short reply to escalate to L2 for high-priority tickets',
  functions: [{ name: 'createTicket', schema: { title: 'string', priority: 'string', metadata: 'object' } }],
});

res.on('function_call', (payload) => {
  // payload is validated against schema on Redwood side
  const body = payload.args;
  fetch('/api/tickets', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(body) });
});

Notes on guarantees: our SDK will perform schema validation server-side and return a structured JSON payload when function-calling is used. For the demo we’ll instrument the trace to show first-token and per-token latency breakdowns.

